WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:05.859
Meet Stamp Page Designer: a free tool for making your own stamp album pages.

2
00:00:05.909 --> 00:00:14.125
You place every stamp, heading and story box yourself, on a two and a half millimetre grid, and every frame prints at its true size.

3
00:00:14.175 --> 00:00:18.132
Version six adds pictures, dividers, new borders and more fonts.

4
00:00:18.942 --> 00:00:21.618
Every visit starts here, on the first screen.

5
00:00:21.668 --> 00:00:26.828
Your last work waits behind Continue, and up to three saved albums sit right below it.

6
00:00:26.878 --> 00:00:28.343
We'll come back to those.

7
00:00:29.150 --> 00:00:34.003
To start a new album, choose the margins first: Classic, or Dense for more room.

8
00:00:34.053 --> 00:00:37.558
Tick the punch-hole margin if your pages go into a binder.

9
00:00:38.361 --> 00:00:46.772
Then pick the paper: Letter, A4, Legal or A3, or one of twelve album page formats, like Scott, Minkus, Davo and Stanley Gibbons.

10
00:00:46.822 --> 00:00:52.852
Choose the spacing between items, across and down, from Tight, five millimetres, up to Wide.

11
00:00:52.902 --> 00:00:56.223
The screen shows exactly how big your grid will be.

12
00:00:57.032 --> 00:01:01.794
Give the album a name, choose how many pages to start with, and press Start designing.

13
00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:03.870
This is the editor.

14
00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:08.430
Along the top are the album name, Undo and Redo, Help, Save album, and Print.

15
00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.871
Below that, there's a coloured button for everything you can add to a page.

16
00:01:13.675 --> 00:01:20.900
Your pages are on the left, the page itself is in the middle, and the panel on the right shows the settings for whatever you select.

17
00:01:21.705 --> 00:01:23.504
Let's start with a Page Header.

18
00:01:23.554 --> 00:01:25.653
Type your title, then pick the font.

19
00:01:25.703 --> 00:01:32.813
There are eighteen built in, each shown in its own lettering, from formal scripts and handwriting to classic book faces.

20
00:01:32.863 --> 00:01:34.484
Then set the size and style.

21
00:01:35.287 --> 00:01:42.028
Choose a height, fit the width to the text, and give it a border, with square or rounded corners, and a single or double line.

22
00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:44.471
Subheaders work the same way.

23
00:01:44.521 --> 00:01:47.737
You can have two per page, for a series name or a plate.

24
00:01:48.539 --> 00:01:49.516
Now the stamps.

25
00:01:49.566 --> 00:01:56.980
Small, Medium, Large and Extra Large each add a frame of that exact size, in the first free spot on the page.

26
00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:00.523
Every stamp gets a number: S1, S2, and so on.

27
00:02:00.573 --> 00:02:04.674
It stays with the stamp and helps you find it, but it never prints.

28
00:02:05.478 --> 00:02:13.564
Select a stamp to type a catalogue caption under it, switch its dashed border on or off, or choose Strips, for a mount with a wider border.

29
00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:17.099
Custom takes any size you type, rectangles too.

30
00:02:18.272 --> 00:02:20.047
And every stamp can be resized.

31
00:02:20.097 --> 00:02:22.048
Select it, and drag a blue corner.

32
00:02:22.098 --> 00:02:30.699
It grows and shrinks in steps of one and a quarter millimetres, up to two hundred and ten millimetres, and it never goes past the edge of the page.

33
00:02:31.501 --> 00:02:33.952
There's also a triangle stamp, as a trial.

34
00:02:34.002 --> 00:02:36.928
Type its base and its height, or drag its corners.

35
00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:40.774
The description box is for your story about a stamp.

36
00:02:40.824 --> 00:02:45.891
Type your text, set the size up to thirty points, and resize the box from its corners.

37
00:02:46.693 --> 00:02:48.401
The Art button adds a picture.

38
00:02:48.451 --> 00:02:53.265
There are twenty-three original drawings: philatelic, postal, and heraldic shields.

39
00:02:53.315 --> 00:02:58.422
Each one takes your border colour, and resizes from its blue corners without stretching.

40
00:02:59.225 --> 00:03:05.439
On a shield, you can add two lions or two unicorns as supporters, and a scroll ribbon with your own motto.

41
00:03:06.241 --> 00:03:10.218
The Divider button adds a line across the page, to separate sections.

42
00:03:10.268 --> 00:03:14.594
Pick a style, from single to double wavy, or a short line with an ornament.

43
00:03:14.644 --> 00:03:16.812
Then choose the weight and the colour.

44
00:03:17.613 --> 00:03:19.568
To move anything, just drag it.

45
00:03:19.618 --> 00:03:21.508
It moves in half-square steps.

46
00:03:21.558 --> 00:03:28.880
Near another item, its edges and centres pull into line, and pink lines show why, while blue numbers show the gap.

47
00:03:28.930 --> 00:03:31.790
Hold Alt, or Option on a Mac, to drag freely.

48
00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:36.664
To move several things at once, Shift-click them, or press Select All.

49
00:03:36.714 --> 00:03:41.718
An arrow key jumps to the next grid line, and Shift with an arrow moves half a square.

50
00:03:41.768 --> 00:03:44.539
Headers and dividers only ever move up and down.

51
00:03:45.345 --> 00:03:48.238
A plain click on one item selects just that one again.

52
00:03:49.041 --> 00:03:54.064
Copy and Paste put a copy right next to the original, exactly one spacing away.

53
00:03:54.114 --> 00:03:56.440
You can even paste onto another page.

54
00:03:57.243 --> 00:04:04.335
If items get too close, or overlap, they turn red, and one line above the page tells you how many items need a look.

55
00:04:04.385 --> 00:04:05.874
Click it to see each one.

56
00:04:06.678 --> 00:04:08.319
Auto-align fixes it for you.

57
00:04:08.369 --> 00:04:13.757
It evens out the spaces, puts every edge on a grid line, and keeps everything on the page.

58
00:04:13.807 --> 00:04:15.690
It never shrinks a single stamp.

59
00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:19.799
If it needs Dense margins to fit, it tells you, and lets you choose.

60
00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:21.767
Changed your mind?

61
00:04:21.817 --> 00:04:24.316
Undo and Redo go back up to ten steps.

62
00:04:25.118 --> 00:04:29.705
Preview shows the page exactly as it will print: no grid, and no colours.

63
00:04:29.755 --> 00:04:31.864
Zoom in and out whenever you like.

64
00:04:31.914 --> 00:04:34.151
Zoom never changes the printed size.

65
00:04:34.954 --> 00:04:41.100
On the left, you can add a blank page, duplicate a whole page, move pages up or down, or remove one.

66
00:04:44.104 --> 00:04:51.214
Page settings, on the right, change the margins, the paper and the spacing for the page you're on, or for every page at once.

67
00:04:52.018 --> 00:04:55.001
The page border decorates every page of the album.

68
00:04:55.051 --> 00:05:01.797
Choose from twenty-three patterns and seventeen corners, in small, medium or large, with your choice of colours.

69
00:05:01.847 --> 00:05:03.132
Or choose none at all.

70
00:05:04.893 --> 00:05:08.223
Switch on page numbers, and choose the number to start from.

71
00:05:08.273 --> 00:05:10.590
They follow your page order automatically.

72
00:05:11.392 --> 00:05:20.070
Then save your favourite setup, with the paper, margins, spacing, caption font and border, as one of three saved settings, ready for any album.

73
00:05:20.873 --> 00:05:23.501
Your work is kept automatically for Continue.

74
00:05:23.551 --> 00:05:28.799
To keep an album for good, press Save album, give it a name, and pick one of three slots.

75
00:05:28.849 --> 00:05:32.311
If all three are full, it asks before it replaces anything.

76
00:05:33.115 --> 00:05:35.725
When you're ready, press Print, Save as PDF.

77
00:05:35.775 --> 00:05:38.022
If two stamps overlap, nothing prints.

78
00:05:38.072 --> 00:05:40.682
The app takes you straight back to fix them.

79
00:05:40.732 --> 00:05:45.034
Always print at one hundred percent, actual size, and never fit to page.

80
00:05:45.084 --> 00:05:47.513
Then check your first print with a ruler.

81
00:05:47.563 --> 00:05:50.958
A thirty millimetre stamp gets a thirty millimetre frame.

82
00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:56.903
Back on the first screen, your work is waiting under Continue, and your album has its own button.

83
00:05:57.755 --> 00:06:01.311
Start fresh begins a brand new project from inside the editor.

84
00:06:01.361 --> 00:06:08.174
It offers to save your work first, asks for a name, and lets you pick the default settings, or one of your saved ones.

85
00:06:08.224 --> 00:06:09.919
Then you get a clean new page.

86
00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:14.572
And if you ever need a hand, Help explains every button and every rule.

87
00:06:15.728 --> 00:06:17.326
That's Stamp Page Designer.

88
00:06:17.376 --> 00:06:21.172
It's free, it's open source, and it runs right in your browser.

89
00:06:21.222 --> 00:06:22.210
Happy collecting!
